From 6f1d637f0f4b9e39db78d7db43a1a52a4fe650a6 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Mon, 12 Oct 2026 05:41:27 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Map: Hide towers button, leaving just the basemap and the
 skyline extents

A new button beside "Display skyline extent" hides every tower marker at once
(clusters and their counts, pins, glows, names, the tower icons, the selected
ring and the time capsule's rings); the basemap, the skyline extents (also as
they shrink with the time capsule year), the city outline and the scale stay.
Hidden layers take no clicks, so a click inside an extent opens its note.
Pressing it again, or picking a tower from search, brings the towers back.
It is per visit, not remembered; ?towers=0 opens the map with them hidden.
The legend keeps only "skyline extent" while the towers are hidden.

Top bar: the button shows "Hide towers" / "Show towers" from 1440 px (the bar
widens to 950 px there, still clear of an open tower panel), the eye alone
below that (bar 850 px from 1300 px); on phones the Filters count is dropped
so the search box keeps its width.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01SxR1iEp4VTVXJNpdqdnZ83
